# <type>[optional scope]: <description>
# Imperative mood, no period, keep subject under 50 characters
#
# [optional body]
#
# [optional footer(s)]
#
# Types:
#   feat:     A new feature (triggers minor version bump)
#   fix:      A bug fix (triggers patch version bump)
#   perf:     A performance improvement (triggers patch version bump)
#   refactor: Code refactoring (triggers patch version bump)
#   docs:     Documentation changes (no version bump)
#   style:    Code style changes (no version bump)
#   test:     Test changes (no version bump)
#   build:    Build system changes (no version bump)
#   ci:       CI/CD changes (no version bump)
#   chore:    Maintenance tasks (no version bump)
#
# Common scopes:
#   core, api, contract, operations, resource, transport, auth, ssr, forms
#   modules, cli, testing, docs, config, build, ci, deps
#
# Use fix only for user-facing defects. Use ci/test/docs/chore otherwise.
# Consumer-visible package changes also require a Changeset.
#
# Breaking changes:
#   Add "BREAKING CHANGE:" in footer or use "!" after type
#   Example: feat!: redesign API (triggers major version bump)
#
# Examples:
#   feat(auth): add OAuth2 integration
#   fix(api): resolve user validation error
#   docs: update installation guide
#   feat!: redesign user API
#
#   BREAKING CHANGE: User API endpoints have changed
